@startuml
title SEQ-23 — Handle VNPay IPN
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
actor "VNPay Sandbox" as Caller
control "PaymentsController" as Entry
control "PaymentsService" as Service
database "PostgreSQL\norders, payments, order_status_history" as DB

activate Caller
Caller -> Entry: Send payment IPN
activate Entry
Entry -> Service: handleVnpayIpn(callback)
activate Service
Service -> Service: Verify VNPay signature and callback format
alt The signature or callback structure is invalid
  Service -> Service: Log safe callback diagnostics
  Service --> Entry: Return provider rejection response
  Entry --> Caller: Return provider rejection response
else The signature and callback structure are valid
  Service -> DB: Lock referenced order and attempt consistently with cancellation and expiry
  activate DB
  DB --> Service: Return stored payment and order details
  deactivate DB
  Service -> Service: Verify reference, amount, VND currency and provider transaction result
  alt The reference is unknown or the amount, currency or transaction details do not match
    Service -> Service: Log safe diagnostics with correlation ID
    Service -> DB: Record reconciliation outcome without settlement
    activate DB
    DB --> Service: Outcome recorded; payment, order and stock unchanged
    deactivate DB
    Service --> Entry: Reject mismatched payment details
    Entry --> Caller: Reject mismatched payment details
  else This callback repeats an already processed notification
    Service -> DB: Record duplicate without repeating business effects
    activate DB
    DB --> Service: Duplicate recorded
    deactivate DB
    Service --> Entry: Acknowledge duplicate; no repeated effects
    Entry --> Caller: Acknowledge duplicate; no repeated effects
  else The result is late, conflicting or no longer applicable to the order or attempt
    Service -> DB: Record safe provider result for reconciliation
    activate DB
    DB --> Service: Result recorded; no order reactivation or settlement
    deactivate DB
    Service --> Entry: Acknowledge recorded non-settling result
    Entry --> Caller: Acknowledge recorded non-settling result
  else The verified successful result applies to the current eligible pending attempt
    Service -> DB: Set attempt SUCCESS and order PAID with history in one operation\nEnforce one success and retain reservation
    activate DB
    DB --> Service: Payment settled and history recorded; no further stock deduction
    deactivate DB
    Service --> Entry: Acknowledge payment success
    Entry --> Caller: Acknowledge payment success
  else The verified non-success result applies while the order still awaits payment
    Service -> DB: Mark attempt FAILED and record provider result
    activate DB
    DB --> Service: Failure recorded; order PENDING_PAYMENT and stock reserved
    deactivate DB
    Service --> Entry: Acknowledge failed attempt; eligible order may retry
    Entry --> Caller: Acknowledge failed attempt; eligible order may retry
  end
end
deactivate Service
deactivate Entry
deactivate Caller
@enduml
